-- title:
--   Separating two supersingular places by a rational level-M' function
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mathtt{LiesOverPrime}$ at $q$, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa, M')$ over $\kappa := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ — where that field is the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, and a place is a proper valuation subring containing the base field and whose maximal ideal is principal — and assume $W$ consists exactly of the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ`. Assume $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathtt{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M' \subseteq \mathbb Q((q))$, generated by the divisor expansions) to $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa, M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathtt{integers}$ together with a surjective residue map onto the $\kappa$-field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with a degree-preserving map on places. Assume further (`hR₀`) that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral, with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally let $s \ne s'$ be two elements of $W$. Then there is a Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathtt{integers}$, such that: for every place $P$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, if $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` is $\ge 0$ then so is $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$; the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subrings of both $s$ and $s'$; and the values $\mathtt{evalAt}$ of that residue at $s$ and at $s'$ are different.
--
--   This is the separation statement for the supersingular locus of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$: two distinct supersingular places are distinguished by the reduction of a single rational level-$M'$ modular function which is Gauss-integral for the constant reduction $R_0$ and regular wherever $j$ is. It is used in the subsequent analysis of the reduced curve at the supersingular points, in particular in the constructions of invariant functions and of node charts on the full-level curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_rational_integral_evalAt_ne_of_ne_ssPlaces.lean

